        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "948bca27-1911-5f03-9ada-2017c19c521d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John André, Benedict Arnold\n- Events: American Revolutionary War, Battle of Bull's Ferry\n- Places: West Point, New York\n- Works: \"The Cow Chace\"\n\nFacts:\n- Benedict Arnold was a general in the American Revolutionary War who first fought for the American Continental Army and later defected to the British Army.\n- John André was born on 2 May 1750 and served as a British Army officer during the American Revolutionary War.\n- The Battle of Bull's Ferry inspired British Major John André to write the satirical ballad \"The Cow Chace.\"\n- John André assisted Benedict Arnold's attempted surrender of the fort at West Point, New York to the British.\n- John André was hanged as a spy by the Continental Army on 2 October 1780 during the American Revolutionary War.\n- Benedict Arnold died on June 14, 1801.",
